course: dictionary
lesson: 16050
title: Vigorously: with energy and force
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Mia shook the bottle vigorously before she opened it.» Shook tells you the action, and vigorously tells you how she did it. She did not shake it a little. She used lots of energy and force.
explain: Vigorously is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done. Look for it after a verb, such as stir, shake, exercise or nod. «Dad stirred the soup vigorously so it would not stick.» Dad stirred hard and with energy.
explain: You can use the same clue check as always. Swap in a meaning and read the sentence again. «The coach told us to exercise vigorously.» Does "with lots of energy" still make sense there? Yes, so you have found the meaning.
fact: Vigorously means with a lot of energy, force or strength.
fact: Vigorously is an adverb: it tells you how an action is done.
fact: The adjective it comes from is vigorous, which means full of energy and strength.
fact: «Shake vigorously» means shake with force, as in shaking a bottle hard.
fact: Vigorous exercise makes your heart beat faster and can leave you out of breath.
exercise: «Mia shook the bottle vigorously before she opened it.» How did Mia shake the bottle? | Just once, by accident | *With lots of energy and force | Gently and slowly | Without making a sound
exercise: The coach says, «Exercise vigorously for ten minutes.» What does vigorously tell you? | Very quietly | *With lots of energy and effort | Sitting down and resting
exercise: «Sam nodded vigorously when he heard the good news.» How did Sam nod? | He did not move his head at all | Slowly and sleepily | *Hard and with lots of energy
test: «Dad stirred the soup vigorously so it would not stick.» What does vigorously mean? | *With great energy and force | Very late at night | Gently | Without touching the pan
test: In the class debate, Priya argued vigorously against the idea. What does vigorously mean here? | Quietly and politely | Not at all | Sleepily | *Strongly, with lots of energy
exam: Jayden says, «I will exercise vigorously after school.» What does Jayden mean? | Sleeping on the sofa | Talking very softly | Sitting still with a book | *Working hard with lots of energy until he is out of breath
